relationships
Joins

1. relationships- “ In a relational database, data is stored across multiple tables, and these tables are connected through relationships.
Instead of repeating the same data again and again in one huge table, we split it into smaller, meaningful tables and connect them using keys (Primary and
Foreign Keys).

Types of Relationships.
1. One-to-One (1:1)
2. One-to-Many (1:N) 🔥 Most common
3. Many-to-Many (M:N)